   corresponding code is itself made available for others to use, with
   credit, under terms ticohq grants with Aaron's/Arkchemy's permission
   -- i.e. reciprocal openness is required before this exclusion is
   lifted for ticohq specifically. This exclusion does not apply to
   this project's own use of separately-licensed third-party emulation
   cores or libraries, which remain governed by their own real,
   independent licenses regardless of this section.

